--Boundary (ID 5SQzKu8TFm5S9W8Dkp8Iuw)
Content-type: TEXT/PLAIN; CHARSET=US-ASCII

I'd like to mainly thank Spider Boardman <spider@orb.nashua.nh.us> 
for his detailed explanation about password encryption on Digital 
UNIX vs. Ultrix, although that only tangentially helped with the 
problem.

I called Digital support, and they stepped me through everything 
again, and it worked.  I think the critical difference was the change 
in security levels.  The Digital Unix "Security" manual says that you 
must run secsetup before secauthmigrate.  I recommend you run this 
immediately before secauthmigrate.  In other words, run secsetup, 
select ENHANCED, reboot to single user mode, and then move the old 
/etc/passwd and run secauthmigrate.  I think the password file change 
is important--I had already merged the password files when I changed the 
security level, and I think that caused a problem.  Even though I 
tried to copy the username:ULT files, it still didn't work.

Thanks to all.  Can I mention that I think this is one of the most 
information-dense mailing lists I've ever been on?

