Hello all, and thanks to all that responded.

RE: Running Sybase on its own partition:
Juergen Bock wrote to say that Sybase can use a RAID partition with no 
problems as it's 'below' the operating system.   He also explained how 
Sybase can also store its data on a mounted filesystem with less 
recoverability in case of a crash due to unflushed write buffers.  If the 
database does not have a lot of activity and the machine is stable, using 
filesystems is nicer because I could use all the normal disk and backup 
tools.

Paul Rockwell and Alan Rollow agreed that RAID partitions should be 
compatible with Sybase for the same reasons.

RE: Disklabel and general partition questions:

Doug Gould and Paul Rockwell and gave me a very good tutorial about 
disklabel - Thanks guys!

Digital sent me a System Admin guide in 2 days!  and it only cost $17 - 
Thanks, 1-800-DIGITAL

