To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: UPDATE SUMMARY: vdump/vrestore
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076327921474

Last year I posted about various problems with vdump/vrestore, the general 
thrust being that vrestore cannot correctly restore files to the state they 
were in at the time of an incremental restore.

I received information that the relevant engineering group were aware of some 
problems, but that there were few customer problem reports. I was encouraged 
to submit my problems through the proper channels.

I sent in a comprehensive exposition of my problems, citing 4 specific bugs. 
One of these was known. The other three were escalated to engineering, and I 
have been told that they will be fixed in a future release.

The QAR numbers are 42783, 42784 and 42785.

Since I firmly believe that the problems are fundamental design flaws rather 
than coding errors, I fear that this is the best I could hope for.

-- 
