Unfortunately, none of them actually solved it.

Digital field service was here, swapping the motherboard and
the tape drive (for the second time). Still the same problem.
Then I did more tests using vdump etc, and it ejects the tape, but
after writing ~4GB.

Makes me rethink the whole scenario, and it turns out that I indeed
have more than 4GB to backup. I believe that NetWorker (NSR) is a bit
misleading when stating "device full, 1600MB of 4000MB used". Actually
it has written 1600MB in the *last* ("current") saveset, but
it had finished off other savesets before.

Anyway, this is what I *think* has happened. It would make sense
for NSR to be more accurate in its error message...
Now, Digital has to come and swap back to the old stuff again :(

I'll post an update should there be any important developments.

-Terje Sten

