Hi,

I'd set up two 3000/400s as NIS master and slave and then had a problem 
getting the automounter to work and getting the maps pushed from the master
to the slave. 

Thanks to Andy Phillips (atp@mssly1.mssl.ucl.ac.uk) for coming up with
the incantation to solve the problem:
   
>> The master maps are /etc/auto.master and /etc/auto.direct for direct 
>> mounting and they're linked to /var/yp/src but if I try to push them
>> to the slave it tells me that it's updated the maps but won't push
>> them. If I log on to the slave and use ypxfr to pull the maps over
>	
>	The solution is to log onto the slave server, and pull the
>    maps across by hand. This has to be done only once, and is 
>    automatic from then on. 
>    e.g. 
>    slave# pwd
>    /var/yp/
>    slave# ./ypxfr -f -h master auto.master
>    slave# ./ypxfr -f -h master auto.home
>    

I did this and everything seems to be working fine now.

