Hello Managers,

I would like to thank the following people for their reponses :_

Kurt Carlson <SXKAC@orca.alaska.edu>
Michael Matthews <matthewm@sgate.com>
alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com
Doug Gould <dgj@omega.rtpnc.epa.gov>
Dave Thompson <THOMSOND@wellington.ecnz.co.nz>

Thanks guys, you really cleared this up for me.

My problem :-

>   a:   131072        0     ADVfs                        # (Cyl.    0 -
>   b:   327680   131072    unused     1024  8192         # (Cyl.  164*-
>   c:  2050860        0    unused     1024  8192         # (Cyl.    0 -
>   g:  1592108   458752     ADVfs                        # (Cyl.  574*-

> / is mounted on rz2a, rz2b is 160M of swap and /var is mounted on rz2g.

> I would like to leave the root and swap partitions as they are, reduce
> the size of the /var partition to around 200M and use the remainder of
> the disk for a new /home filesystem.


The solution :-

1. Reduce the size of g and leave its offset unchanged.
2. Use partition h for the new filesystem.
3. Make partition h's offset to be g's offset + g's size.
4. Make h's size all that's left.

Here's a copy of the new disklabel :-

8 partitions:
#        size   offset    fstype   [fsize bsize   cpg]
  a:   131072        0     ADVfs                        # (Cyl.    0 -
164*)
  b:   327680   131072    unused     1024  8192         # (Cyl.  164*-
574*)
  c:  2050860        0    unused     1024  8192         # (Cyl.    0 -
2569)
  d:   327680   131072    unused     1024  8192         # (Cyl.  164*-
574*)
  e:   327680   131072    unused     1024  8192         # (Cyl.  164*-
574*)
