From tru64-unix-managers  Sat Jan 13 18:02:11 1996
From: Greg King <king () reston ! ans ! net>
Date: Sat, 13 Jan 1996 18:02:11 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Power Management, Firmware Rev Levels RZ29B
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076327921235


I had asked about a cryptic note pertaining to a power
management problem with Rev 0007 of the RZ29B firmware.
The note mentioned a specific bit that could be changed
if the Rev 0007 firware was used.  Conclusion: upgrade
to the Rev 0014 firware.  Despite the non sequential
jump, there are no Rev 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, or 13 versions
so if you have Rev 0007 you are only one back.  You can
check your rev level with SCU:

scu>
scu> set nexus bus 1 target 1 lun 0
scu> show device
scu> ........

Rev 0014 is the current firware rev level, local field
service can install it, and it is installed with the 
SCU utility.  Be sure the back up your drives first
and insure that the process is not interrupted or the
drives will have to be shipped back to be re-enabled.

Greg

Thanks to Stan Huhman, huhman@ee.deere.com 
          Daniel.Clar@supelec.fr (Daniel Clar)
          Digital's CSC and our local field service

>Because of other problems we had with the version 0007 firmware, we 
>upgraded all of ours to rev 0014.  This takes care of the power
>management issues, which as I recall has to do with the spindle powering
>down after some period of inactivity.  There should be an article about this
>in the list archives, which is where I first learned of the problems.
>
>Upgrading the firmware is a simple matter once you have the download
>set and a few simple instructions.  It uses the SCU utility and takes
>only a couple minutes per drive.  I got the firmware from DEC's CSC
>with help from my local field engineer. 
>Stan Huhman
