The answers:

_______

OPEN3D
_______

3d xserver that implements PEX and OpenGL

OPEN3D is OpenGL port to DEC OSF; 


OPEN3D - software support for modern versions of Digital Unix (newer
than 2.0) to be able to run the more sophisticated graphics
hardware/software.   See release notes on the Open 3D layered product
on the DU layered products CR-ROM set.

OPEN3D = DEC Open3d Support for SGI GL compatible Library calls and 
graphic 3D accelerated cards  support
see setld -i | grep DWS

OPEN3D

  Open-3D drivers for accelerated graphics cards (like ZLX, PXG for the
turbochannel, I have no clue what for the PCI based machines). The layered
products is Open3D.


OPEN3D
--
	Provides support for OpenGL, the standard 3-D rendering
	library used on e.g., IBM, SGI, DEC, HP, etc. Useful if you're
	displaying 3-D images (AVS, etc).


OPEN3D	- This is the supporting software for graphics hardware (PHIGS,
OpenGL, PEX, etc.), including drivers


OPEN3D

Open3D is the software that provides support for the 3D graphics API's
PHIGS and OpenGL.


__________

MMS-RT
__________

Multi media services runtime

MMS-RT is Multimedia Services Runtime; comes standard on all workstations - enables audio and video 

MMS-RT - Multi-Media Services - Run-Time support.  License to use the
audio and video capabilities of DEC Unix (on-board sound card and
vidio services on Alpha 3000 Mod 300X, like we use here, for
instance).  See release notes on the MMS-RT layered product on the DU
layered products CR-ROM set.


MMS-RT = Mutli media Support Run time modules , for sound and video tools and libs
Needed for new generation mutlimedia PCI based AXP machines equipped with sound card.
see setld -i | grep MME

MMS-RT

	Multi-media services runtime. Lets you use the multi-media
	extensions (alphavcr, decsound, etc).



MMS-RT	- Multimedia Services, Runtime.  Inlcudes API, drivers for video and
audio hardware, applets.



MMS-RT

This is the Multimedia Services for Digital UNIX runtime license. Allows you
to play audio and video.


__________

COMIQ!
__________

Video conferencing software - runs on top of MME

COMIQ!

	I think this is the license for the Communique
	video-conferencing tool. I didn't get one with my video system
	so don't know.

COMIQ!	- Communique! groupware and API from InSoft. Not sure on all the
componets it includes, but pretty sure it's just shared whiteboard and API.

COMIQ!

I think that this is the license for the bundled version of Insoft's 
COMMUNIQUE! software (network-based multimedia conferencing).



