Date: Wed, 03 Jan 1996 20:07:19 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: NFS problems between Ultrix and Digital Unix
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076327921053


Thanks to all who replied to my query.  It turns out that the problem
was as follows:

	/jim8 was not mounted on the dir /jim8, but on a softlink /jim8
which was linked to the dir /wren8.  A similar situation existed for the
other partitions I was trying to mount.  Apparently, nfs doesn't like
mounting partitions which are really links.  I'm not sure how this all
happened in the first place, as I have not always been the sysadmin for
this system.  Changing the mount points on jim to be real dirs solved
the problem.

Cheers,
--Lee
